  "title_sha256": "ae39eb1e92fa806df189c768c1478a53dfb54a2cc9769a9f2301ca7921e3eb04",
  "scope": "Two desktop replays through the shooting tutorial with stock Proton Experimental, MangoHud, conventional temporal antialiasing and reduced effects. Input-to-milestone spans include time outside the game viewport.",
  "differences": "The previous run recorded Unreal PSOs and started with warm driver and translation caches. The grouped-pixel run used the default reduced-effects settings and 57 more preparation entries following a host reboot. Both used NVIDIA 620.70.06. The grouped run loaded matching graphics libraries privately for the test. The driver and Proton cache contents differ when DXIL changes. These observations compare the two runs as played.",
  "method": "Each present ends at the MangoHud CSV creation time plus its elapsed nanoseconds. Match Unreal chase and level-streaming messages on their UTC timestamps. The tutorial window starts when an actual game capture first showed both prompts. Use only a focused, mapped game on the powered, visible workspace with no overlapping fullscreen client. Hyprland polled each 0.5 seconds. Exclude 0.6 seconds on either side of each focus change. Whole-frame metrics require both endpoints to fall inside the window. Mean FPS is complete frame count divided by their summed duration. The foreground present-rate and clipped hitch duration also count the visible portion at each boundary. Percentiles use nearest rank. Discard invalid frames and post-close presents.",
